Z||000010||Monkeyman||10-08-2000||11:58 PM||||How freaking fast do you guys intend to go?  I paid about $400 for my Beretta upgrade and can stop almost as fast as my wifes new ABS equipped Cavalier, better probably.  And I don't even have the new SS brake lines on yet.  Is this for show/ego or does anyone really think that they need $2000 brakes?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Archie||10-09-2000||12:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>How freaking fast do you guys intend to go?  ....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I used to know Wabash, Indiana. <P>Wabash, Indiana was a neighbor of mine (Mishawaka, IN)<P>Sir, Chicago is no Wabash, IN.<P>I'd insert smiley face here if I knew how.<P>The question you should have asked is....."How freaking fast do you guys intend to STOP?"<P>In Wabash, defensive driving means missing that buggy..... up here defensive driving is being able to stop and accelerate fast enough that the locals can't draw a bead on you.<P>Ok, just joking...... I agree with you, IMHO, dollar for dollar, the Beretta upgrade is a pretty good deal. <P>But I have put big wheels on my F-40, Finale and Blue Chop Top cars and I NEED the 11.25" rotors just so you have something to look at between the spokes of the wheels. BIG wheels + dinkie rotors = no go.<P>BTW, many 15" wheels WILL fit under the 11.25" brakes, I have 15" Momo's on the Finale and they clear just fine.... so take that!!!!<P>another smiley thing here<P>Archie||||reg||6
Z||000012||Monkeyman||10-09-2000||06:24 AM||||Archie--If you want smilies, just look to the left of the reply screen.  Click on "Smilies Legend".  That should get you through.  We don't have many buggies around here, but I know what you're saying.  I drove a truck for many years so I know all about Chicago driving.  I agree that you need bigger go and stop when driving in Chicago (or any big city).  Always some fool who wants to cut you off or tailgate.  I hadn't thought about the looks angle much.  I plan on getting 17" rims at some point, but I'll have to stay with my dinky Beretta brakes.  No way I can justify (or afford) that kind of money just for looks (unless you'd like to donate a set <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). ||||reg||1
